ing revoked offers that is that is  extremely unusual in in a in a standard  college year but the latest data shows  an increasing number of employers  surveyed are revoking full-time offers  and internships are at risk to 20  percent of employers surveyed  revoking offers Dow Jones which  publishes the Wall Street Journal has  postponed most of its internships until  next year  Edwin Koch says a critical aspect of the  internship is developing a cultural  connection between the intern and the  company I'm not sure how well you can  measure the cultural thing as companies  increasingly shift to virtual recruiting  job seekers will have to learn how to  stand out in a virtual setting and in a  newly packed field students who  graduated in 2009 experienced a similar  challenge when they entered the toughest  job market in decades when the college  recruiting market started to open up in  2010 the 2009 grads would not treat it  as new college graduates they were if  they were lumped in with the employees  who grown unquote had experienced the  few studies that have been done shows  that when you graduate in a period like  this the ramifications the negative  ramifications  unfortunately continue with you for most  of your employment career the recruiting  numbers are changing by the day but  coach says the when it comes to hiring  or revoking offers many employers are  taking a wait-and-see attitude that's  when we saw a significant change in  terms of some clients ramping up Patrick  Burrell is the CEO of true blue a  recruiting and staffing agency clients  that we saw just falling through the  floor in terms of their volumes were  hospitality tie providers hotel clients  our Burrell says that when companies are  scaling down temporary workers are often  the first to get cut but that they're  often the first part of the workforce to  recover after a recession employers use  temporary workers to augment their  workforce I wouldn't be surprised if we  saw employers using  temporary workers more than they have in  the past on the try before you buy type  of arrangement  Edwin Koch suggests getting into the  workforce is the first step the student  would always ask is it is it better to  take any old job or is it better to wait  the employers that I lose with on those  presentations would always tell that it  was better to put something on your  resume it take what you can get even if  it is volunteering as two and there is  no income associated with it despite the  outlook students like kata are adapting  to this changing markets really just  allowed me to open my mind a little bit  more the possibilities and realize that  you know just because you have a plan  doesn't mean that that's set in stone  that's exactly how it's gonna happen  you
 

